{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/LangChain Network Model Adapter.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/LangChain Network Model Adapter.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"lang chain network model adapter lang chain network model adapter","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/LangChain Network Model Adapter.md","fileName":"LangChain Network Model Adapter.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"LangChain Network Model Adapter","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 18:30\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Network AI Application Architecture]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Network AI Application Architecture","ainetworkingcookbook.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/LangChain Network Model Adapter.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/LangChain Network Model Adapter.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"lang chain network model adapter lang chain network model adapter","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/LangChain Network Model Adapter.md","fileName":"LangChain Network Model Adapter.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"LangChain Network Model Adapter","heading":"LangChain Network Model Adapter","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A LangChain model adapter gives application code a consistent invocation surface for a local Ollama model or a hosted chat model. The adapter holds model identity and endpoint details so the network-analysis function can focus on constructing input and consuming output.\n\nThis abstraction makes substitution and composition easier, but different models still vary in message semantics, context size, latency, and output quality. Switching an adapter is therefore an integration change that requires task-specific tests. It should not be assumed that identical prompts produce equivalent network guidance across providers.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Networ